{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const INTERRUPT_BINDING_VERSION: 1;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts#L79","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts:79"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire version of "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/InterruptBinding.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"InterruptBinding"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The binding is the only part of an AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" that this package\nclaims — it rides in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" under\n"},{"type":"link","href":"INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and tells the resume path how to\ncorrelate an answer back to a paused run. Producers stamp "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v"},{"type":"text","value":"; readers\nreject any version they don't understand rather than duck-typing the fields."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That matters because an AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" is a shared envelope. Another\nproducer — a workflow engine projecting a durable approval, a third-party\nagent — can legitimately put its own binding in the same envelope. Versioning\nmakes \"not mine\" a clean rejection instead of a partial match that resumes\nagainst the wrong owner."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst INTERRUPT_BINDING_VERSION: 1;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts:79](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts#L79)\n\nWire version of [InterruptBinding](../type-aliases/InterruptBinding.md).\n\nThe binding is the only part of an AG-UI `Interrupt` that this package\nclaims — it rides in `metadata` under\n[INTERRUPT\\_BINDING\\_METADATA\\_KEY](INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY.md) and tells the resume path how to\ncorrelate an answer back to a paused run. Producers stamp `v`; readers\nreject any version they don't understand rather than duck-typing the fields.\n\nThat matters because an AG-UI `Interrupt` is a shared envelope. Another\nproducer — a workflow engine projecting a durable approval, a third-party\nagent — can legitimately put its own binding in the same envelope. Versioning\nmakes \"not mine\" a clean rejection instead of a partial match that resumes\nagainst the wrong owner.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: INTERRUPT_BINDING_VERSION\ntitle: INTERRUPT_BINDING_VERSION\n---\n\n```ts\nconst INTERRUPT_BINDING_VERSION: 1;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts:79](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/interrupts.ts#L79)\n\nWire version of [InterruptBinding](../type-aliases/InterruptBinding.md).\n\nThe binding is the only part of an AG-UI `Interrupt` that this package\nclaims — it rides in `metadata` under\n[INTERRUPT\\_BINDING\\_METADATA\\_KEY](INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY.md) and tells the resume path how to\ncorrelate an answer back to a paused run. Producers stamp `v`; readers\nreject any version they don't understand rather than duck-typing the fields.\n\nThat matters because an AG-UI `Interrupt` is a shared envelope. Another\nproducer — a workflow engine projecting a durable approval, a third-party\nagent — can legitimately put its own binding in the same envelope. Versioning\nmakes \"not mine\" a clean rejection instead of a partial match that resumes\nagainst the wrong owner.\n"}
